# Figma is read through the MCP

The live file `ks-MarketingSite` (`IBO39siJYDhiCRtuLWUTW2`) is the design
intent. Every Figma URL in a comment or a chat message exists to be opened
through the Figma MCP — for a new section, a refresh, an asset export, or a
one-value fix.

## The protocol

Before building or changing anything designed, run on the node:
`get_metadata` (structure and sizes), `get_variable_defs` (bound tokens), and
`get_design_context` (fills, radii, per-variant values, asset URLs). Read the
nodes fresh at build time — never from memory of an earlier read, a screenshot,
a prior extraction, or the previous implementation.

**If the Figma MCP is unreachable, stop.** Do not approximate from a screenshot
or carry values over. Report which server, tool, and node failed and wait.
Acceptable recovery: the server is unauthenticated → run its `mcp_auth`; it
needs Figma Desktop → ask the user to open the file; the node id is malformed
or deleted → ask for the URL again. "The data file probably still matches" is
not on the list.

## Node reads have known blind spots

- `get_metadata` returns position and size only — no radius, fill, or
  interactivity. Any cell that might be ornament or a control is read per-node
  with `get_design_context`.
- Inside a Figma grid auto-layout, a child's metadata `x`/`y` can be stale.
  Verify geometry against rendered bounds (`absoluteBoundingBox`) through the
  console bridge before committing it. Carousel frames overflow their anchors;
  verify against the in-frame clip.
- Stroke alignment produces ±0.5/±1px artifacts (a frame at x −0.5, insets
  reading 23/31/33 where the design means 24/32). Transcribe the intended whole
  value, not the artifact.

## The console bridge

The Figma console MCP runs JavaScript inside the live file and returns what the
read tools cannot: rendered bounds, effect values, verbatim SVG exports of
vector geometry. Use it to verify transcription, to export icon geometry, and
whenever cached metadata is suspect.

## The file can be wrong — never build the error

Frames occasionally carry a mis-bound variable, a stray ornament cell, stale
copy. When a node disagrees with its siblings or the established pattern, flag
it to design instead of building it. Loop: flag → design fixes in Figma or
records a decision → re-read the touched nodes → record the resolution in a
comment at the value (node id, date, what changed). Building a known error "to
match the file" is never correct.

## Component-set reads

- Read every variant of a set (sizes, chromes, states) — never scale one
  variant to produce another.
- Check `width / t` and `height / t` at the anchor: whole ticks or designed
  half-ticks are structure; anything else is material.
- When a set's cells equal the anchor ticks (32/48/64/80/112), the design is
  tick-riding drawn at 1:1 — read those px as `1t`.

## Re-extract the token layer before building

Token values come from the Figma variables API and the text styles, not from
the file's rendered frames. Re-extract before a new section build (see
`docs/reference/tokens.md` §9 for the procedure); regenerate `tokens/type.css`
from `type-styles.json` with `node scripts/generate-v2-type-css.mjs`. Silent
design-side changes flow through the tokens with no component change.

## What the MCP does not know

The MCP does not know the codebase. It exports whatever the file contains,
including assets and shapes already implemented, named by SHA hash. Before
committing an export: search `icons.tsx`, `media.ts`, and `public/media/`;
rename to descriptive kebab-case or delete the duplicate.
